Name the CONTAINER a controller view was added to, not just its class.

Three editors added to the SAME container means the last one added is in front. Three added to
DIFFERENT containers means they are separate screenfuls and something one level up decides which
container is shown. The class name alone cannot tell those apart, and both were live theories.

It answered immediately for iA Writer: three editor scroll views, three DIFFERENT NSView containers,
2 adds, 2 adds and 9 adds. They are separate screenfuls.

THE COMMENT ALSO RECORDS A NESTING THAT MISLED ME. addSubview logs, then _insertSubview: calls
removeFromSuperview which logs again, then the window is set and the appearance fires. So a log
reading "add X, remove X, appear X" is ONE add, not the application taking X away. I read an earlier
run as the application removing editors and it never removes one at all, which is also why
viewWillDisappear correctly never fires: nothing is ever taken off screen.
--- a/AppKit/NSView.m
+++ b/AppKit/NSView.m
@@ -1883,10 +1883,18 @@
     if (view == nil || view->_ciderViewController == nil)
         return;
 
-    fprintf(stderr, "CIDER_VIEW move %s %s(%p) controller=%s other=%s\n", what,
+    /* THE SUPERVIEW POINTER, not just its class. Three editors added to the SAME container means the
+     * last one added is in front; three added to DIFFERENT containers means they are separate
+     * screenfuls and something else decides which container is shown, and the class name alone
+     * cannot tell those apart (#194).
+     *
+     * NOTE THE NESTING: addSubview logs, then _insertSubview: calls removeFromSuperview which logs
+     * again, then the window is set. So "add X, remove X" in that order is ONE add, not the
+     * application taking X away. */
+    fprintf(stderr, "CIDER_VIEW move %s %s(%p) controller=%s other=%s(%p)\n", what,
             object_getClassName(view), view,
             object_getClassName(view->_ciderViewController),
-            other != nil ? object_getClassName(other) : "(nil)");
+            other != nil ? object_getClassName(other) : "(nil)", other);
     fflush(stderr);
 }
 
